  "results": [
    {
      "id": "q_the_emergency_council_meeting_1",
      "question": "What are the wizards asking the council to do in the emergency meeting-and what's the catch?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown"
      ],
      "context_must_hits": [
        "arcane lockdown",
        "wards"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 0.5,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "wizards' college": "synthesis_gap",
        "arcane lockdown": "hit",
        "wards": "synthesis_gap",
        "tradeoff": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The wizards are pushing for a citywide arcane lockdown to contain the cult\u2014but the catch is it could isolate parts of the city, strain defenses, and put civilians (and unprotected players) at risk.\n\nFrom CANON and OBSERVED city facts, the proposed plan is an **arcane/magical lockdown** (the city: \u201cProposed arcane lockdown\u201d; \u201cPlanned magical lockdown\u201d) aimed at stopping the cult, which is operating via hidden routes and tunnels beneath the city.\n\nThe catch:\n- **Isolation risk (OBSERVED)**: \u201cAt risk of having parts isolated if key tunnels or access points are sealed,\u201d which could trap civilians or disrupt response efforts.\n- **Defense strain (CANON)**: The \u201cintegrity of the city's defenses is a matter of concern,\u201d so forcing a lockdown may stress already \u0915\u092e\u091c\u094b\u0930 systems.\n- **Collateral danger (CANON via players/defenses)**: Magical defenses and traps may target those without proper protections (e.g., amulets), potentially including the players.\n- **Political/social fallout (OBSERVED/CANON)**: With unrest over tolls and ongoing protests, a lockdown could escalate tension while the council is already divided on crisis response.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Proposed arcane lockdown; integrity concerns\n- Operational Status: Planned magical lockdown; city under threat from cult\n- Governance: Council actively debating crisis response\n- Geography: Hidden passages and tunnels complicate containment",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_session_12_council_chamber_roster",
      "question": "Who's actually in the council chamber for the Session 12 fight with the Wolf?",
      "strict_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "semantic_verdict": "fail_incomplete",
      "must_hits": [
        "thalia",
        "wolf",
        "guards"
      ],
      "semantic_must_hits": [
