        "ephanna"
      ],
      "context_support_ratio": 1.0,
      "failure_surface": "synthesis_gap",
      "stage_loss_tokens": {
        "bonogo": "evidence_gap",
        "caelynn": "evidence_gap",
        "thalia": "hit",
        "wolf": "hit",
        "guards": "hit",
        "ephanna": "evidence_gap"
      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The fight in the council chamber involves the Players, the Wolf, Thalia, and multiple Guards; council members are not explicitly confirmed as present in the projection.\n\nBased on OBSERVED and CANON facts:\n- **Players (group)** are present and actively engaged; they recount their story to the council and become combat participants.\n- **the Wolf** is explicitly in the **Council Room** and is the central adversary of the encounter.\n- **Thalia** is present with the Wolf (\u201cWolf is standing at Thalia\u2019s shoulder\u201d) and becomes involved in combat, initially acting under his influence.\n- **Guards** are present and escalating the situation: some are already in the chamber, and additional guards are \u201cbeing drawn here as reinforcements,\u201d with several actively attacking or engaging.\n\nNotably, **council members themselves are not explicitly confirmed** in the projection as being physically present during the fight, despite the setting.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Geography: Large circular chamber, central table, high ceilings, hidden trapdoor.\n- Defenses: Magical wards, illusory walls, rune activations affecting the battle.\n- Atmosphere: \u201calmost the entire room is lit up by Fireball,\u201d disheveled, chaotic.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q_longmont_campaign_general_notes_1",
      "question": "Who are the Shepherds, and what god or power do they answer to?",
      "strict_verdict": "pass_updated",
