      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: Headmaster Tinkerbright represents the wizards; he views the cult as a dangerous perversion of magic and pushes for aggressive arcane detection and containment (including a lockdown).\n\nHeadmaster Tinkerbright (OBSERVED role: representative of the Arcane; CANON faction: Wizard\u2019s College) is the wizard voice on the council.\n\nHis angle on the cult is strongly interventionist:\n- CANON: He sees the corrupted meat as a perversion of magic and takes the threat very seriously.\n- OBSERVED: He is eager to deploy Wizard\u2019s College resources to detect and counteract the cult, including magical runes to identify corruption and even a planned magical lockdown of the city.\n- CANON/OBSERVED: He supports using detection spells and arcane methods to locate cult activity.\n\nIn short, Tinkerbright frames the cult as an arcane contamination problem and advocates for wide-reaching magical surveillance and containment measures.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Head of the Wizard\u2019s College; arcane representative on council  \n- Alignment toward cult: Treats it as a severe magical threat/perversion  \n- Strategy: Detection (runes, spells), resource deployment, possible citywide lockdown  \n- Disposition: Brilliant, inventive, but deeply troubled by the cult\u2019s magic",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
