      },
      "stale_hits": [],
      "global_stale_hits": [],
      "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead\u2014**\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\u2014with Bonogo taking the head, overriding earlier escape attempts.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**: he both \u201cescapes\u201d and becomes \u201cInvisible,\u201d attempting to flee via a secret passage, but also has the terminal condition **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d** The decisive, most current outcome is supported by **ent_bonogo (role): \u201cRemoved the Wolf\u2019s head to transport it.\u201d** That terminal outcome supersedes any prior escape or invisibility\u2014those occurred during the fight but did not persist.\n\nSo at fight\u2019s end: the Wolf is not fled; he is dead, physically separated (head taken), and no longer an active agent.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Identity: the Wolf (second-in-command, cultist, saboteur)\n- Final Physical Condition (OBSERVED): **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d**\n- Prior Status (OBSERVED, superseded): Invisible, attempting escape through secret passage\n- Involved Party: Bonogo removed and kept the head\n- Narrative State: Threat neutralized physically, but implications (cult, plans, Speak with Dead) remain active through the remains",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
