      "answer": "TL;DR: There\u2019s no evidence in the projection that Thalia is corrupted like the guards; her behavior is tied to The Wolf\u2019s influence (he \u201corders Thalia to attack the group\u201d), which suggests something different, but it\u2019s not explicitly defined.\n\nBased on the available facts:\n- **OBSERVED:** The Wolf \u201corders Thalia to attack the group,\u201d and his history includes \u201cBetrayal (as presented to Thalia).\u201d\n- **OBSERVED:** Corrupted guards consistently show a defining marker: \u201can oily sheen to their eyes.\u201d\n- **OBSERVED:** The Wolf himself also has \u201can oily sheen to his eyes,\u201d linking him to that corruption.\n- **No facts** mention Thalia having this oily sheen or any physical corruption markers.\n\nSo, as written, Thalia is **not confirmed to be corrupted in the same way as the guards**. Her actions are clearly influenced or directed by The Wolf, but whether that\u2019s magical control, deception, or partial corruption isn\u2019t specified in the projection.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Thalia: Ordered by The Wolf to attack; influenced by his \u201cbetrayal\u201d narrative (OBSERVED)\n- Guards: Corruption marked by \u201coily sheen to their eyes\u201d (OBSERVED)\n- The Wolf: Has the same oily sheen; actively manipulates others (OBSERVED)\n\nIf you need a definitive ruling, the projection doesn\u2019t lock it in\u2014you have room to decide the exact nature of Thalia\u2019s condition.",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
