      "answer": "TL;DR: The council room actively interferes via arcane traps (force bursts + paralysis), illusion effects that disorient, and environmental hazards like falling debris\u2014especially targeting anyone without the proper amulets.\n\nThe room itself is a weaponized space:\n\n- **Arcane trap bursts (CANON/OBSERVED):** These trigger against those without amulets, dealing **2d6 force damage** and potentially **temporarily paralyzing** targets. Guards are largely exempt because **trusted guards wear amulets**.\n- **Selective targeting (CANON):** The trap system distinguishes allies via amulets; the **Players** are at risk if they don\u2019t have them.\n- **Illusion effects (CANON):** The party has been **disoriented by illusory walls/illusion spells**, which can distort positioning and line of sight mid-fight.\n- **Falling debris (OBSERVED):** The environment forces characters to **dodge falling debris hazards**, adding constant pressure and repositioning.\n- **Ambient feedback (CANON):** The room\u2019s **wall hum changes** signal triggers or escalations, hinting at incoming effects but also adding tension.\n- **Rune alarms (OBSERVED via Guards):** These can escalate the encounter by alerting defenders and locking things down.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Arcane traps keyed to amulets\n- Hazards: Force bursts, paralysis, falling debris\n- Control: Illusions affecting perception and movement\n- Feedback: Audible hum signaling changes\n- Security: Rune alarms tied to guard response",
      "embedding_similarity": null
