      "answer": "TL;DR: Delay gives the cult time to advance their plan\u2014using hidden routes and council influence\u2014to sabotage the city and potentially complete their summoning, pushing the city closer to disaster.\n\nIf the council stalls, the biggest threat is **the cult acting unopposed**.  \n- CANON: The cult is already **using hidden routes** and has **influence in the council**, so inaction directly benefits them (the cult).  \n- CANON: Their goals include **completing their summoning**, **accessing the heart of the city**, and **sabotaging or corrupting the cauldrons**.  \n- OBSERVED: The city is already **\u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d** (the city).\n\nOn top of that, the city is vulnerable:  \n- CANON: **Less fortified parts** and **defense integrity concerns** (the city).  \n- CANON: Infrastructure like **sewers and hidden passages** is already in play (the city, the cult).\n\nSo what \u201cbites you\u201d is a compound failure: infiltration + delay = the cult advances beneath notice, potentially triggering a major event (e.g., summoning or widespread corruption) before the council commits to any plan.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Weak points; integrity concerns; hidden routes exploitable  \n- Governance: Council indecision; cult influence \u062f\u0627\u062e\u0644 council  \n- Operational Status: \u201cbrought closer to disaster by each failed or unresolved debate\u201d  \n- Threat: Cult pursuing summoning and sabotage within city infrastructure",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
