      "answer": "TL;DR: The Council Room should feel tense and compromised\u2014signs of illusion magic, corrupted guards, and the aftermath of the Wolf\u2019s defeat, including his **Decapitated; head removed from body** state.\n\nAfter the fight, the room reflects both chaos and something more insidious beneath the surface:\n\n- The Wolf\u2019s body is present in a grim state: **Decapitated; head removed from body** (OBSERVED, the Wolf physical_condition), making the violence undeniable and immediate.\n- Several guards\u2014especially those checked\u2014show **an oily sheen to their eyes** (OBSERVED, Guards physical_condition), signaling corruption that hasn\u2019t ended with the fight.\n- The space likely still carries the aftermath of confusion: the Wolf was known to create illusory duplicates (CANON, the Wolf defenses), so lingering uncertainty or disrupted positioning (overturned chairs, misdirected attacks) fits what just happened.\n- Guards are **visibly tense** and struggling to maintain order (OBSERVED, Guards mental_state & goals), suggesting the danger isn\u2019t over.\n- The broader context presses in: this is a council under pressure, mid-crisis about the city\u2019s safety and corruption (OBSERVED, city governance & operational_status).\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Defenses: Illusion magic used (Wolf duplicates)\n- Physical Condition: **Decapitated; head removed from body** (Wolf), oily-eyed guards\n- Atmosphere: Tense, unstable, distrustful\n- Factions/Corruption: Guards visibly affected and compromised",
