      "answer": "TL;DR: Before the council fight, the Wolf is an active, deceptive infiltrator manipulating events; after, he\u2019s a broken, exposed figure who ends up **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d** with clear signs of corruption.\n\nBefore the council fight (OBSERVED + CANON):\n- The Wolf is a **saboteur and cultist**, \u201csecond-in-command\u201d of the guard, actively **deceiving the council** and steering decisions.\n- He relies on **illusion magic (illusory duplicates)** and misdirection, creating confusion and avoiding direct confrontation.\n- Operationally, he\u2019s **mobile and evasive** (invisibility, escape routes, secret tunnels).\n- Mentally, he\u2019s calculating but already showing cracks: **sensed danger**, under pressure, and tied to betrayal.\n\nAfter the council fight (OBSERVED):\n- His state collapses into desperation: **\u201cbegging for someone to release him,\u201d \u201cbegging to be killed,\u201d \u201cfeels regret.\u201d**\n- His corruption is explicit: **\u201cWolf has an oily sheen to his eyes.\u201d**\n- His arc ends in a terminal outcome: **\u201cDecapitated; head removed from body.\u201d**\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Enemy \u2192 defeated adversary\n- Mental State: Controlled/deceptive \u2192 desperate/regretful\n- Physical Condition: Illusion-using infiltrator \u2192 \u201cDecapitated; head removed from body\u201d\n- Alignment Context: Hidden cult sympathizer \u2192 exposed, visibly corrupted (\u201coily sheen to his eyes\u201d)",
      "embedding_similarity": null
    },
